# The display must be named by host (TCP): these X libraries have no
# local transport. "noname" is Atari System V's default node name; use
# yours (uname -n) if you changed it.
# 1024x768 in 256 colours fits every card.  24-bit colour (add -depth 32)
# needs the card's full 4 MB, jumpers A0 and A1 closed: on a card set up
# for 2 MB the server stops ("needs more than the card's 2 MB") and xdm
# with it.  Xatw -listmodes lists the modes.
noname:0 local /usr/x11r6/bin/Xatw :0 -mode 1024x768 -vt 1
